{"id": 77, "ts": 1780443707.3116896, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fA is the strongest overall fit. While we\u2019ve heard concerns about a \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d attitude and resistance to new ideas, A\u2019s core strengths directly address the most safety\u2011critical criteria: the ability to anticipate dangerous situations (operational reliability), to see complex connections (technical competence), excellent spatial vision (attention to detail), and very good leadership qualities (crew cooperation). In contrast, Candidate\u202fD, although technically strong and responsible, exhibits a hot temper and a know\u2011it\u2011all demeanor, which pose higher risks for crew harmony and stress resilience on long\u2011haul flights. Given the balance of strengths versus concerns, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fA."}
