{"id": 82, "ts": 1780443740.6849933, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s point about Candidate\u202fA\u2019s ability to anticipate dangerous situations and his strong spatial vision, but I remain uneasy about the unfriendly attitude and unhealthy habits that could undermine crew cooperation and long\u2011haul reliability. Candidate\u202fD, on the other hand, consistently demonstrates the core safety\u2011critical traits we need: he takes responsibility seriously, solves problems exceptionally well, concentrates intensely, and responds adequately to unexpected events\u2014exactly the mix of technical competence, decision quality, and stress resilience required for long\u2011distance operations. While his moodiness and loner reputation raise a flag for crew interaction, those concerns are outweighed by his proven responsibility and problem\u2011solving record, especially when compared with the communication and teamwork gaps evident in Candidates\u202fA,\u202fB, and\u202fC. Therefore, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fD for the position."}
