{"id": 86, "ts": 1780443776.509231, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fA is the strongest overall fit.\u202fHis ability to anticipate dangerous situations and to see complex connections directly supports the reliability and technical competence we need for long\u2011distance operations, while his excellent spatial vision enhances attention to detail.\u202fMoreover, his very good leadership qualities are a clear asset for crew cooperation in the cockpit.\u202fThe concerns raised about him being a \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d and not open to new ideas are noteworthy, but we have no evidence that these traits have translated into poor professional communication or unsafe decision\u2011making, and his leadership could mitigate potential friction.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fD, while strong on responsibility and problem\u2011solving, exhibits a hot temper and is perceived as a know\u2011it\u2011all\u2014behaviours that risk crew tension, especially under the high stress of international flights.\u202fGiven the balance of strengths and the relative severity of the concerns, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fA."}
